 هذا حلال وهذا حرام وما أشبه ذلك من افترائهم","mentions":[]},{"verses":["22:30"],"words":["قَوْلَ ٱلزُّورِ"],"type":"reports","speaker":"النبي صلى الله عليه وسلم","stance":"reports","claim":"A report says the Prophet, after the dawn prayer, stood facing the people, declared false testimony equal to associating partners with God, and recited this verse; al-Razi gives no grading.","anchor":"عن النبي صلى الله عليه وسلم أنه صلى الصبح فلما سلم قام قائما واستقبل الناس بوجهه","mentions":[]},{"verses":["22:30"],"words":["قَوْلَ ٱلزُّورِ"],"type":"interpretation","speaker":"author","stance":"reports","claim":"Other interpretations of false speech are lying and slander.","anchor":"وثالثها الكذب والبهتان","mentions":[]},{"verses":["22:30"],"words":["قَوْلَ ٱلزُّورِ"],"type":"interpretation","speaker":"أهل الجاهلية","stance":"reports","claim":"The pre-Islamic pilgrimage chant counted as false speech because it affirmed a partner for God while claiming that God owned that partner and whatever it owned.","anchor":"وقول أهل الجاهلية في تلبيتهم لبيك لا شريك لك إلا شريك هو لك تملكه وما ملك","mentions":[]}]}
